From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:42:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch 2 games: in its app folder's eglantine/,
 started by it and back to it

PS5-ECAM (PPSA99360) carries this program as eglantine/eboot.bin and starts its Switch 2 games in it
with LoadExec, as it starts its Switch games in Eden's (eden/).
- Its folder is the app's eglantine/ (/app0/eglantine, /system_ex/app/PPSA99360/eglantine,
  /data/homebrew/PPSA99360/eglantine), its sandbox PPSA99360's, its data /data/eglantine. The game
  files folder is the Switch side's (ecam_layout::Eden, as Eden's program and the launcher choose
  it: /data/eden, or <drive>/eden), so its keys and firmware serve both; while that has no keys, a
  standalone EglantinePS5's /data/eglantineps5 is used as it is when it has them.
- The arguments PS5-ECAM starts it with are in /data/eglantine/launch-request.txt too, one a line:
  on the console LoadExec does not carry them (PS5-ECAM's #67). Taken once with filesystem access
  (forwarded_launch.h, TakeLaunchRequest), else the program's own arguments.
- Where main returns (a game PS5-ECAM started has ended, or this launcher was left), it LoadExecs
  PS5-ECAM's eboot (--return <eboot>, then /app0, the system's mount and /data/homebrew); a home
  screen tile's --exit-after-game still closes it. A game that stops with an error opens this
  launcher, which says why, and Circle on its home screen goes back. After a crash it starts itself
  again (/app0/eglantine/eboot.bin); a game PS5-ECAM starts after a crash is started all the same.
- etaHEN's app jailbreak is asked first, as PS5-ECAM asks for its own process; the Lapy helper is
  built for PPSA99360 and looked for in /app0/eglantine, then /app0.
